title: 'txpool: hold the transaction pool as a trait object instead of a wrapper'

doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |-
      `TransactionPoolWrapper` existed only to give the boxed transaction pool a sized type that
      could travel through the generic `Arc<Pool>` parameters used across the service builder. The
      pool is now referenced directly as `Arc<dyn FullClientTransactionPool<Block>>`, which
      `TransactionPoolHandle` aliases, so the extra layer of forwarding is gone.

      `FullClientTransactionPool` no longer carries a `Client` type parameter. All three of its
      associated types are projections that discard the client, so `Hash`, `InPoolTransaction` and
      `Error` are spelled out in terms of `Block` alone. Naming them that way required widening the
      public API of `sc-transaction-pool`: `sc_transaction_pool::error` and
      `sc_transaction_pool::Transaction` are now exported.

      As a consequence `BuildNetworkParams`, `BuildNetworkAdvancedParams`, `SpawnTasksParams` and
      `GenRpcModuleParams` no longer carry a transaction pool type parameter, and none of them
      constrain the client on the transaction pool's behalf any more: the `BlockIdTo` and
      `TaggedTransactionQueue` bounds that only existed to build a pool are gone from
      `build_network`, `build_network_advanced`, `spawn_tasks`, `gen_rpc_module` and from the
      cumulus `build_network`.

      The client capabilities needed to actually construct a pool are spelled out once as
      `sc_transaction_pool::ClientForTransactionPool`, which is used by the transaction pool
      `Builder` and internally by `FullChainApi`, `BasicPool::new_full` and
      `ForkAwareTxPool::new_full`. It does not pin the `BlockIdTo` error, so a hand written client
      is free to choose its own.

      Components that keep the pool behind an `Arc` stay generic over the pool type, so an
      alternative pool implementation is still free to define its own error and in-pool transaction
      types. They accept unsized pools now, which is a relaxation and needs no changes on their
      side.

      Migration for nodes outside this repository

      - `sc_transaction_pool::Builder::build` hands back an `Arc` already, so drop the surrounding
        `Arc::from(..)` at the construction site.
      - `TransactionPoolHandle<Block, Client>` is `TransactionPoolHandle<Block>` now.
      - Drop the transaction pool type argument where `BuildNetworkParams`,
        `BuildNetworkAdvancedParams`, `SpawnTasksParams` or `GenRpcModuleParams` are named
        explicitly, since the block type now determines it.
      - Add `?Sized` to any generic parameter that holds the pool behind an `Arc`, because
        `TransactionPoolHandle` is a trait object and no longer has a statically known size.

